==========================================================================================
MEDIATION DECOMPOSITION SUMMARY (FOR ESSAY)
==========================================================================================

Window Total Effect (c) First Stage (a) Direct Effect (c')  Indirect Effect (a×b)
   30d     +2.34pp (ns)     +10.84pp***       +0.04pp (ns)  2.77pp [-7.31, 13.05]
   90d     -0.18pp (ns)     +10.84pp***       +0.01pp (ns)  0.15pp [-9.91, 10.06]
  180d     -1.32pp (ns)     +10.84pp***       -0.06pp (ns) -1.42pp [-11.37, 8.44]

==========================================================================================
INTERPRETATION FOR MEDIATION PARAGRAPH
==========================================================================================

First stage (a): The FCC mandate successfully forces immediate disclosure.
  Coefficient: +10.84pp (p < 0.001)
  This is the 'mechanism working' part.

Direct effect (c'): The FCC effect net of timing is near zero and not significant.
  Coefficients: +0.04pp, +0.01pp, -0.06pp (all ns)
  No governance activation independent of timing.

Indirect effect (a×b): The timing channel runs negative.
  30d: 2.77pp [-7.31, 13.05] (CI crosses zero - descriptive, not significant)
  90d: 0.15pp [-9.91, 10.06] (CI crosses zero - descriptive, not significant)
  180d: -1.42pp [-11.37, 8.44] (CI crosses zero - descriptive, not significant)

Mediation logic:
  The mandate forces timing (+10.84pp).
  Timing co-moves with lower turnover (b negative).
  Net path is therefore negative.
  But net effect is null because the negative indirect path
  is offset by a near-zero direct path.

Caveat: The b coefficient is selection-contaminated.
  For FCC firms, timing is mandated (exogenous).
  For non-FCC firms, timing is chosen (endogenous).
  Causal claim is clean only for FCC-induced variation.
  Report mediation as descriptive evidence on mechanism,
  not as causal direct-versus-indirect decomposition.

